<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MANYWATERS_COLOR_SUPPORT_1 v1 — coloured water and coloured slime, ten TerrainDefs.

  MECHANISM (verified against RimWorld 1.6 source, not guessed):
  - `TerrainDef.DrawColor` (from the `<color>` field) is passed straight into
    `GraphicDatabase.Get<Graphic_Terrain>(texturePath, Shader, ..., DrawColor)` for
    EVERY edgeType including `TerrainWater` (`Verse/TerrainDef.cs:433`) — one texture,
    N `<color>` variants is vanilla's own convention (`Terrain_Floors_StoneTile.xml`:
    six colours on one `TileStoneBase` texture; this repo's own `AshLadder.xml`,
    `JawaSaltCrust.xml`). `(R,G,B)` is 0-255 int syntax, confirmed against that file.
  - Colour MULTIPLIES the texture (same law as `Palettes/sandscoured.md`): these RGB
    values were chosen to read as a visible tint against the existing water/slime
    ramps, not as paint. They are FRESHLY AUTHORED for this item, not sourced from
    any mod XML or screen calibration — record any owner change to them here.
  - ⚠️ The design's open question — whether `<color>` survives the `Map/WaterDepth`
    overlay material, which `TerrainDef.cs:448` creates with no colour parameter at
    all — is UNVERIFIED offline. First live test is the FIRST thing painted on the
    quicktest grid (see the item file); if the tint washes out under the depth
    overlay, the fallback is a recoloured copy of `WaterShallowRamp.png` per colour
    (still XML-only) rather than blocking the rest of the slice.

  WATER — `RM_Water_<Colour>`, ParentName="WaterShallowBase" (vanilla, always
  present), texture is vanilla's own `WaterShallowRamp` — same asset `WaterShallow`
  itself uses (Data/Core/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Water.xml). No cross-mod texture
  dependency, no MayRequire needed.

  SLIME — `RM_Slime_<Colour>`, ParentName="WaterShallowBase" (NOT
  ParentName="AB_LiquidSlime" — that would make the whole def unresolvable, not just
  cosmetically wrong, the moment Alpha Biomes is absent; XmlInheritance can leave a
  dangling ParentName). Instead each def is gated with `MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes"`
  (Alpha Biomes' real packageId, confirmed live: `.../workshop/content/294100/
  1841354677/About/About.xml` line 32) at the TerrainDef tag itself, so the whole
  node is skipped — never loaded, never magenta — when AB is inactive. The texture
  path (`Terrain/Surfaces/AB_SlimeRamp`) is AB's own asset
  (`.../1841354677/1.6/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_GelatinousSuperorganism.xml:129`,
  confirmed present under AB's `1.6/` folder — resolving the design's open question
  of whether AB ships 1.6 content: it does). `driesTo` points at AB's own
  `AB_SlimeGrass`, safe under the same gate.

  AMBIENT BUBBLES — each slime def carries `throwFleckChance` + `fleckData` pointing
  at the matching tinted `RM_Fleck_Steam_<Colour>` (Defs/FleckDefs/
  RM_ColoredSteam.xml), the exact vanilla mechanism Odyssey's own `HotSpring` uses
  (`Data/Odyssey/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Water.xml:128-136`, consumed by
  `SteadyEnvironmentEffects.cs:171`) — zero C#, per the design's own finding. Water
  rows get no flecks; the ambient-bubble ask was slime-specific.

  SCOPE NOTE — the design's §3 recipe describes the SIX-cell grid per row (one
  untinted control + five tinted) and separately states "Author count: 12
  TerrainDefs + 5 FleckDefs". Read literally that is inconsistent with its own
  recipe (5+5=10 new defs, not 12) UNLESS "12" counts the two CONTROLS too — vanilla
  `WaterShallow` and AB's own `AB_LiquidSlime`, both already-existing defs that get
  painted alongside these ten, not re-authored here. That is the reading this pass
  took: 10 new TerrainDefs below + the two pre-existing controls painted at test
  time = 12 terrain defs total on the grid. Recorded here because the owner's
  ruling did not resolve the arithmetic, only the "skip the gate test" scope call.

  Not authored here (explicitly deferred, per the design's §2 and the owner's
  ruling): the `temporary=true` canal-flood siblings and the FluidDefs that would
  let FluidCanals carry these colours — those follow once the owner picks which
  colours stay.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════ WATER — WaterShallowRamp, tinted ══ -->

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RM_Water_Rust</defName>
    <label>rust-tinted water</label>
    <description>Shallow water carrying enough dissolved iron oxide to run the colour of old blood. Nothing about it says which mine or wreck it drained through.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <driesTo>Gravel</driesTo>
    <color>(168,92,58)</color>
    <tags>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RM_Water_Verdigris</defName>
    <label>verdigris water</label>
    <description>Shallow water tinted teal-green by dissolved copper salts — the colour a bronze hull turns after long enough underwater.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <driesTo>Gravel</driesTo>
    <color>(70,168,140)</color>
    <tags>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RM_Water_Amber</defName>
    <label>amber water</label>
    <description>Shallow water gone gold-brown with dissolved resin or spice residue. Smells sweeter than it should.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <driesTo>Gravel</driesTo>
    <color>(198,150,60)</color>
    <tags>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RM_Water_Violet</defName>
    <label>violet water</label>
    <description>Shallow water stained a deep violet by something living in it, or something that used to.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <driesTo>Gravel</driesTo>
    <color>(120,80,168)</color>
    <tags>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RM_Water_Chalk</defName>
    <label>chalky water</label>
    <description>Shallow water clouded pale by dissolved minerals — the milky look of runoff off a limestone seam.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <driesTo>Gravel</driesTo>
    <color>(200,196,178)</color>
    <tags>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════ SLIME — AB_SlimeRamp, tinted, MayRequire Alpha Biomes ══ -->

  <TerrainDef MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes" ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RM_Slime_Rust</defName>
    <label>rust-tinted slime</label>
    <description>Liquid slime carrying the same iron stain as the rust-coloured water nearby. Whatever produces it drank from the same source.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/AB_SlimeRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/AB_SlimeRamp_Polluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <driesTo>AB_SlimeGrass</driesTo>
    <color>(168,92,58)</color>
    <throwFleckChance>0.25</throwFleckChance>
    <fleckData>
      <fleck>RM_Fleck_Steam_Rust</fleck>
      <velocitySpeedRange>0.01~0.5</velocitySpeedRange>
      <velocityAngleRange>-90~90</velocityAngleRange>
      <rotationSpeedRange>-50~50</rotationSpeedRange>
      <solidTicksRange>1~3</solidTicksRange>
      <scaleRange>1.5~3</scaleRange>
    </fleckData>
  </TerrainDef>

